---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const pageTitle = "about";
---
<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
	<p>
		i am currently a master's student studying cybersecurity engineering at washu (in st. louis). 
		i also completed my undergrad at washu, where i majored in computer science. broadly, my research 
		and professional interests lie in creating safe, secure, and robust autonomous systems. i've had the 
		privilege of exploring these interests through my involvement in 
		<a href="https://engineering.washu.edu/faculty/Hussein-Sibai.html" target="_blank">prof. hussein sibai's</a> 
		research group. so far, i've primarily worked on developing novel conformal perception contracts for occupancy-based 
		safe planning in closed-loop autonomous driving settings.
	</p>
	<p>
		this summer, i'm working as an ml engineer intern at washu's <a href="https://di2accelerator.wustl.edu/" target="_blank">
		di2 accelerator</a>, where i'm helping design and deploy the infrastructure for a decentralized agentic network capable
		of supporting a variety of autonomous agents in sharing information and coordinating on complex tasks. part of my work
		also involves training new agents and providing an intuitive interface for non-technical users to interact with 
		and contribute to custom agents to the system.
	</p>
	<p>
		<em>
			i wrote this website in <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank">{Astro.generator}</a> and deployed it on <a href="https://vercel.com/" target="_blank">vercel</a>; it's been
			both a fun and pragmatic way to pick up some web development skills. here's the <a href="https://github.com/amaan-19/website" target="_blank">source code</a> if you're interested!
		</em>
	</p>
	<p><em>last updated: june 17 2026</em></p>
</BaseLayout>